      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (55%):</strong> F1 proxy fatalities in GCC trigger additional US retaliation cycles; F5 crude breaches $120 7DMA as dual-chokepoint supply shock accumulates; F2 ceasefire fails before Aug 1 and no de-escalation mechanism engages.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (30%):</strong> No GCC fatalities in the 72h window (F1 fails); Hormuz stays closed (F3 fails) but US-Iran strikes stabilize at current tempo; F4 framework eventually negotiated September–October as mediators persist through two or three cycles.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (15%):</strong> Qatar-Egypt-Pakistan ceasefire accepted by both sides (F2 succeeds before Aug 1); US strikes pause; IRGC modifies Hormuz closure; shipping recovery begins (F3 succeeds) and Brent 7DMA remains below $120 (F5 fails).</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Following the Darkhovin nuclear plant strike by Israeli F-35s on July 19, IRIB and Tasnim ran continuous coverage of the Supreme Leader's emergency session with the Supreme National Security Council. State media carried SNSC chairman Shamkhani's statement that Iran retains the full legal and military right to respond to nuclear facility strikes, framing the Israeli operation as a violation of the Non-Proliferation Treaty. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>Kayhan and Tasnim published commentary characterizing the Bürgenstock MOU as a Western deception, with editorials noting that Iran's concessions on IAEA inspector access were "answered with nuclear facility strikes." State media did not attribute the Darkhovin strike to any single state in initial hours, despite IDF confirmation of the operation; this editorial choice follows a pattern of tactical ambiguity in Iranian media coverage of retaliatory escalation decisions. IRNA framing of the July 12 Hormuz closure has consistently emphasized Persian Gulf historical sovereignty rather than operational military capability. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>Mojtaba Khamenei delivered a nationally televised address on July 20 declaring that Iran "will not negotiate under attack." IRNA and Press TV carried the address without editorial qualification, and Tasnim published the full transcript. Unnamed Iranian diplomatic sources, cited by Axios and Iran International on July 21, described Iran's acceptance of the Qatar-Egypt-Pakistan ceasefire framework as "not excluded" if the US paused strikes for 72 hours — a gap between the public leadership position and the back-channel conditional framing that is the central variable for the September 30 framework window. → supports <span class="cite">F4</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

